WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.166 --> 00:00:02.535
-Our next guest
is a sportscaster

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.537
and television personality
whose podcast "Up &amp; Adams"

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.140
airs weekday mornings at 11:00
on FanDuel TV.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.241
Please welcome to the show
Kay Adams, everybody.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:11.444
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:17.950 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:24.423 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.426
Welcome to the show, Kay.
How are you?

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:28.828
-I feel like I'm dreaming, Seth.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.296
Well, this -- We are dreaming,

00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:33.366
because you were on your way
to Las Vegas

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.167
to start doing
your Super Bowl shows.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.870
-Terminal one, LAX.
-Terminal one.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.838
So you were on your way.
You were in the airport

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.007
when we reached out and asked
if you would come to our show.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.408
-I'm on the escalator.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.677
I look down, and my amazing
publicists were like,

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:45.878
"Do you want to do Seth Meyers?"

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.014
And I was like,
"Uh, let me turn around."

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.050
I went up, I turn,
I go to terminal five,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.785
and ipso facto,
yada, yada, yada, here I am.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.687
-Well, we're so happy
to have you.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.956
And I should note,
I've watched your show,

00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:00.559
and I feel like you seem to be
a person who's very good

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:01.928
at juggling
a lot of balls at once.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.163
And even today, when I went
back to say hello to you

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:05.398
in your dressing room,

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.266
you were on a Zoom
with Trevor Lawrence.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.001
So you were interviewing...
-Yes.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.804
-...the Jaguars quarterback

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.105
when I came to talk
about interviewing you.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.873
Very impressive.
-Well, it's Super Bowl week.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.942
So, you know, the people
who cover sports and football,

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.378
it's our Super Bowl, too.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:19.778
So there's Radio Row
and there's all this.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.148
So I have this insane set.
Everything's built.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.483
And then all these guys
are showing up.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:24.583
But I'm not there
because I'm here today,

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:25.985
which I'm happy about.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.119
But, yes, I had an interview
with Trevor Lawrence.

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:28.488
You were kind enough
to say hello.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.189
And maybe I'll talk
to Kenny Pickett,

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.757
your Steelers quarterback.
-Thank you very much.

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.859
It'd be nice if you talked to
some Steelers for me, as well.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.562
There's not a lot of talk
about the Steelers right now.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.896
-We'll see if they
ever get to the Super Bowl.

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:38.030
-Not a lot of chatter.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.833
So I would say
that Super Bowl week

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.167
is already mayhem
no matter where it is.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.402
But this year
it is in Las Vegas,

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.204
which is always mayhem.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.640
What is your expectation
for what a Super Bowl

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.142
in Las Vegas
is going to be like?

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.843
-I was at F1 a couple
of months ago.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.779
-Okay.
-And they were so welcoming.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.047
The city had it organized,
on lock,

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:56.949
but I feel like
if you're going to Vegas,

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.618
it's that, like,
Kevin McCallister

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.253
"Home Alone" moment
with the schematic.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.421
Like, you get it on the table,
you roll it out,

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.323
and you have to plot out
where you're going

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.926
and your energy
and your coffee and whatever,

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.527
because it's going to be
absolute madness,

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:11.697
all the stars, and then,
of course, Usher, halftime.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.299
Anybody excited about that?

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:16.702
-Now, you feel like we're not
talking enough about usher?

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.672
-I feel like -- Yeah.
-I think you're right.

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:22.074
-I'm a big fan of undersell,
overdeliver.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:23.810
It's just a life mantra.

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:26.245
And I feel like we're talking
Taylor Swift, which is amazing.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.513
And she's taking over.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.415
And, you know, last year
was epic with Rihanna.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.451
Then before that, we had,
you know, Doctor Dre out in L.A.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:33.886
But I feel like --
and I'm going to go ahead

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.655
and say my bold take here --
this is going to be

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:38.658
a top-five-all-time
Super Bowl halftime show.

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:39.959
He's going to put on the party.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.461
I think people forget
how many hits he has,

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.064
banger after banger, and it
will be amazing and a party.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.532
-That's very exciting.
-Yes.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.901
-Now, you're doing
two-hour shows

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.871
as opposed to a usual one-hour
show the whole week in Vegas.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.406
And how many --
It seems to me

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:56.976
that you have a ton of guests
when you do your show.

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:58.511
You're just rolling in
one after the other.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.746
Is that by design?

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.748
Do you like just
the sort of mayhem

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.382
of talking
to as many people as possible?

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.284
-Yeah, because if I don't,
then I have to talk.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.652
-Oh, interesting.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:07.987
-You like to come and, like,

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:09.488
you know, do your,
"Oh, this is what I think."

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.056
But then I want to get
people's stories out of them.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.558
-Yes, absolutely.
-I think I've learned

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.460
just in covering sports,
I love the interview.

00:03:15.527 --> 00:03:16.996
And you do an amazing job.

00:03:17.062 --> 00:03:19.898
Like, I feel warm and comfy
and amazing here.

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:22.468
And I think there's
a real craft to it.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.470
And so I really enjoy
getting stories out of people.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:27.439
I mean, we have Gronk
on my show every week.

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:29.708
We have -- We had Will Ferrell
come on and surprise him.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:32.077
Like, we have as many guests
as possible to make it a party.

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:35.048
-Now, Gronk -- you are doing
a live commercial with Gronk

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.415
at the Super Bowl.
-Yes.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.950
-Now, Super Bowl commercials
are already a big deal,

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.185
but a live
Super Bowl commercial,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.586
that has the added pressure,

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.788
I don't need to tell you,
of being live.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.157
[ Laughter ]
-Well --

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.425
-And this is Gronk
will be trying --

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.159
Is Gronk trying to kick
a field goal again?

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.194
-He is, but I haven't really
thought about it that much.

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:51.530
-Oh, I'm sorry. I didn't mean
to remind you that it was live.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:54.067
-Now I'm getting
a little more nervous.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.035
No, he is.
He missed it last year.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.537
-Yes.
-It was bedlam last year.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.072
So now it'll be
a little more organized.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.541
I'm going to be the reporter.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.476
It is live during
the Super Bowl.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.244
And then somehow
I'm going to have to be

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.678
airlifted into the stadium

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:08.113
so I don't miss
any of the action.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.782
-Oh, my goodness.
-But it's live.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.451
Like, it's happening.
He's kicking. He's practicing.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.752
-Do you think he makes it?
-Of course I think he --

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:14.987
I thought he'd make it
last year.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.155
But everybody can go to FanDuel

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:18.090
and guess if he makes
or misses it.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:21.060
And you can get a split
of like $10 million on FanDuel.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.795
So go and cheer Gronk on,
everybody.

00:04:22.861 --> 00:04:24.997
-Alright, and now
what about prop bets?

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.566
Now, for those who don't know,
prop bets are the sort of bets

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.869
you wouldn't naturally think of
as far as, like,

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:32.438
who's going to win or over/under
or score the first touchdown.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.073
-Right.
-What's a good prop this year?

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.642
-Is it weird that I'm obsessed
with, like, the Gatorade?

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.477
Like, I'm in the Gatorade.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:39.645
-Oh, whether it gets dumped?

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.146
-No, what color
it's going to be.

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:42.815
-Interesting.
-That's, like, a mega --

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.917
-I can't believe you're allowed
to bet on something like that.

00:04:44.983 --> 00:04:46.519
-It's so nerdy,

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.921
but you don't understand,
the people over at FanDuel,

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:52.191
the abacuses, like, you know,
the tallying everything,

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.527
they keep track
of what color the Gatorade is

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.929
for these teams all season long,
as best as they can,

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.265
to sort of make the algorithm
for what it will be.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:01.700
The most popular is purple.
That was last year.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.636
Red's a long shot,
which I'd bet on,

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:06.239
because I think the logos
are both red, so that's great.

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.008
Um, and, yeah,
lime yellow, whatever.

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.409
Like, just go over
and have some fun.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.911
Prop bets are sort of
my favorite.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:14.413
One interesting thing
I saw today on FanDuel,

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.816
or I heard,
was that Travis Kelce

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:20.152
is the most bet-on player
to win Super Bowl MVP

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:23.656
by like twice as much
as any of the quarterbacks,

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:24.990
who are, of course, favored.
-Gotcha.

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:26.459
-And FanDuel
thinks that's Taylor.

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.727
-Yeah, well, of course it is.
Yeah.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:30.029
-No, seriously. Yeah.
-And this is a big deal.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.597
I mean, the Taylor of it all

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:34.266
has been a very exciting sort of
through line to the season.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.702
And now there's a drama because
she's going to be in Japan.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:40.539
And the ambassador of Japan

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.708
basically wrote a letter
saying she's going to make it.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.177
-Yes.
-This seems like --

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:47.046
I mean, the fact
that it's reached

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:49.582
the level of, like,
geopolitical affairs.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.951
-It seems like a good
prop bet over at FanDuel.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:54.152
Will she or will she
not make it?

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:55.420
I'm so happy for them.

00:05:55.487 --> 00:05:57.222
I'm so happy for Travis,
of course.

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:58.958
I've covered him in my career.
-So happy.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.459
-And, like, you know, anybody --

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.161
You know, we love love.
Don't we love love?

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.562
-We love love.
-We love love.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.797
-Who doesn't love love?

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:06.232
-I would love to see
a little confetti angel.

00:06:06.298 --> 00:06:07.699
-You know what I'm betting on
on FanDuel?

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:08.901
I'm betting on love,
'cause love always wins.

00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:09.969
-And I'd bet on love.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.570
-Love always wins, FanDuel.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:12.905
But I'm going to bet
on it nonetheless.

00:06:12.971 --> 00:06:16.175
-Love, Super Bowl MVPs,
and Gatorade colors.

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:17.810
-Now, you're from Chicago.
-Yes.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:20.078
-But you're a Bengals fan.
Talk me through this.

00:06:20.145 --> 00:06:22.882
-Um, well, I was on, um,

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:25.451
a national television show
covering all 32 teams,

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:28.253
and I sort of picked before
the big Joe Burrow season

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.789
that led them to a Super Bowl
but eventual loss --

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:32.524
um, I picked them
to make the playoffs

00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:33.926
when nobody was picking them.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:36.161
Is this, like, a Steelers thing?
Is this weird?

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:37.496
-No, I find it --

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:39.398
This is not a Steelers thing.
-Okay.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.968
-And I think Joe Burrow's great
and I really like his vibe.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.970
And I wish he didn't
play for them.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.972
-I hear you.
-But I guess I'm wondering,

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:49.908
how do you -- did you have
family who was curious

00:06:49.975 --> 00:06:51.077
as to why you were, like,

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:53.179
leaving the Bears
for the Bengals?

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:55.180
-I mean, I don't think
anybody is curious

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:57.450
about why you leave the Bears
to support another team.

00:06:57.517 --> 00:06:59.084
-Now, see, now you're just
piling on the hurtfulness.

00:06:59.151 --> 00:07:01.220
-Since 1985.
-Yes.

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:03.455
-Uh, basically,
I liked Joe Burrow.

00:07:03.522 --> 00:07:04.623
He was healthy.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.258
I felt like nobody
was picking them.

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:08.260
Everyone was picking every
other team in the division.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.629
And I think when you're
a fan base that's downtrodden

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:12.832
and not talked about,
if you're given a little love,

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:15.767
sometimes when you just show a
little faith in somebody, Seth.

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:18.237
You've got to bet on love.
And that's what happens.

00:07:18.303 --> 00:07:20.439
-I think we started
talking about football,

00:07:20.505 --> 00:07:22.107
but I really hope
that the takeaway from this

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:23.675
is just the strength
of relationships.

00:07:23.742 --> 00:07:26.044
-I feel like I should lay down
and do a therapy session here.

00:07:26.111 --> 00:07:28.013
-Let's get into it.
The longer you do this,

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.782
I imagine, you must have better
relationships with the players.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:32.551
They must have more confidence

00:07:32.617 --> 00:07:33.953
that they're going to have
a good time with you.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.054
Has that been one of the coolest
parts of your career

00:07:36.121 --> 00:07:37.456
is just realizing
that at this point,

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:38.691
people know what
they're going to get

00:07:38.757 --> 00:07:40.726
when they talk to you
and enjoy it more?

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:43.395
-I think I've always
approached my job

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:45.530
in covering football

00:07:45.597 --> 00:07:48.867
as authentically
as a fan as possible.

00:07:48.934 --> 00:07:50.135
It's not always easy.

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:53.406
You have to tackle
tough topics, of course,

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:55.541
but I'm very celebratory
about the game.

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:57.409
I get juiced.
I'm standing on my couch.

00:07:57.476 --> 00:07:58.677
Like, I have
my favorite players.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:00.679
I grew up loving Matt Forte.

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:03.648
I just said that to make up
for the mean Bears stuff.

00:08:03.715 --> 00:08:05.384
I love Devin Hester.

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:08.020
Yeah, so I just have
a real appreciation

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:09.321
for what these guys do.

00:08:09.388 --> 00:08:11.123
I mean, I took
a pickleball lesson

00:08:11.189 --> 00:08:12.391
for the first time
this past week,

00:08:12.457 --> 00:08:13.926
and I'm not athletic at all.

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:15.361
So the fact that these guys can
do what they do on this level

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:17.029
is so incredible
mentally and physically.

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:18.397
-I almost forgot to ask.

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:20.099
You took a pickleball lesson
for the first time.

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:22.535
You're going to play in a
pickleball tournament in Vegas.

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:24.069
I assumed because
you were playing

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.071
in a pickleball tournament,
you knew what you were doing.

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:28.107
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:30.409
Get this. First of all,
I live in L.A. now.

00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:31.977
I love New York.
I'm a New Yorker.

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:33.578
I don't want to be in L.A.,
so whenever anybody asks me,

00:08:33.645 --> 00:08:35.080
and they ask a lot,
"Want to go play pickleball?"

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.082
I just say no, just to be
sort of a curmudgeon about it.

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:39.017
-Yeah. Of course.
-Yeah, very Larry David of me.

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:40.786
-Do you want to remind people
you're a New Yorker?

00:08:40.852 --> 00:08:43.021
-I just -- No, I don't want to
go learn about pickleball

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:45.191
or what the kitchen is
or any of that nonsense, right?

00:08:45.258 --> 00:08:47.793
So then I get asked by Smirnoff

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.862
to do this
pickleball tournament,

00:08:49.928 --> 00:08:51.563
and they pair me
with Vernon Davis,

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:52.631
Super Bowl champion.

00:08:52.697 --> 00:08:54.033
-The San Francisco 49er
tight end.

00:08:54.099 --> 00:08:57.002
-I'm five foot tall,
like, on a good day.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:59.705
Like, I got big heels on.
He's what, 7'9".

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:03.441
I'm going to get toppled on this
baby tennis court, first of all.

00:09:03.508 --> 00:09:04.910
Then I'm a liability.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:07.179
Then we're taking on
Scheana Shay and her husband.

00:09:07.246 --> 00:09:08.414
So those Vanderpumpers,

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.549
like, they understand
what cameras are.

00:09:10.615 --> 00:09:12.251
They're not going to shrink
in the light.

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:15.053
People are like, "Oh, but you
have an athlete next to you.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.122
You're going to just --
You're going to beat everybody."

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:19.158
Do you really think, like --
You think Scheana Shay's

00:09:19.224 --> 00:09:21.059
returning a serve
to Vernon Davis?

00:09:21.126 --> 00:09:23.128
No, I'm going to get
exposed and pelted.

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:24.796
-Yeah.
-I'm going to be the scapegoat.

00:09:24.863 --> 00:09:26.799
The whole time I'm going to be
getting worked on this court.

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:30.236
-Now, can I go on FanDuel
and bet against you on this?

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:33.139
-Yes. Safe bet.
Well said by you.

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:34.707
Get this, though.
Whoever loses or wins,

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:36.242
I think I have to
go up against --

00:09:36.309 --> 00:09:38.910
Like, Saweetie and Lance Bass
is the other pairing, so...

00:09:38.977 --> 00:09:40.012
-I don't know.

00:09:40.079 --> 00:09:41.480
-I need to get
my stuff together.

00:09:41.546 --> 00:09:43.415
-I'm starting to realize
you came to New York

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:44.916
not because you wanted
to be on this show.

00:09:44.983 --> 00:09:46.451
You just wanted to get away
from that pickleball match.

00:09:46.518 --> 00:09:47.954
-I did. You know what
I really wanted to do?

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.522
It was an easy yes,
because I just feel like

00:09:49.588 --> 00:09:51.523
you can't be in Vegas
for more than 48 hours.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:55.327
So anything to limit
my Vegas time was the move.

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:57.028
-And you did your show
in Zoom anyway.

00:09:57.095 --> 00:09:58.798
You got it figured out.

00:09:58.864 --> 00:10:00.332
But best of luck.
Have a great time out there.

00:10:00.398 --> 00:10:02.134
And thanks so much
for being here.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.602
You guys, that's Kay Adams,
everybody.

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:07.173
"Up &amp; Adams" airs weekday
mornings at 11:00 on FanDuel TV.

00:10:07.239 --> 00:10:10.476
We'll be right back with Nana
Kwame Adjei-Brenyah, everybody.

